#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100521 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "41b7d83f-3b9b-556c-9e49-13df9c3b597e" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Functions Containing the Natural Logarithm"}] :question/id #uuid "8ea17e06-1248-510c-9e71-c57da0cb0d02" :question/math-academy-id "e-14405" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int \\dfrac{3}{x \\sqrt{\\ln x}} \\, \\textrm{d}x}$." :question/worked-solution "Let's set $u = \\ln x$. Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}= \\dfrac 1 x\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm{d}u=\\dfrac 1 x\\,{\\textrm{d}x}\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫\\frac{3}{x\\sqrt{\\ln x}}dx &= 3∫\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\ln x}} \\cdot \\frac{1}{x}dx \\\\\n&= 3∫\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}du \\\\\n&= 3∫u^{-1/2}du \\\\\n&= 3 \\cdot 2u^{1/2} + C \\\\\n&= 6\\sqrt{u} + C \\\\\n&= 6\\sqrt{\\ln x} + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100522 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa28f5c4-135e-576a-baa0-68c41b5139f6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Functions Containing Other Logarithms"}] :question/id #uuid "1579f932-6e7f-5daa-b001-54a9f6c236ad" :question/math-academy-id "e-14406" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{\\log^2_3 x}{x} \\,\\textrm d x$." :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac{(\\log_3 x)^2}{x} \\,\\textrm d x\n$$\n\nLet $u=\\log_3 x$. Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = \\dfrac{1}{x\\ln 3}\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\\ln 3\\,\\textrm d u = \\dfrac 1 x \\textrm d x\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫((\\log_{3} x)^{2})/(x)dx &= ∫(\\log_{3} x)^{2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{x}dx \\\\\n&= ∫u^{2} \\cdot \\ln 3du \\\\\n&= \\ln 3∫u^{2}du \\\\\n&= \\ln 3 \\cdot \\frac{1}{3}u^{3} + C \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}\\ln 3(\\log_{3} x)^{3} + C \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}\\ln 3\\log_{3}^{3} x + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100523 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37a7aff6-d1b2-5383-bb26-aa6363594b05" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Definite Integrals"}] :question/id #uuid "d2f49acf-ed91-510d-a0f1-41c50eeef9e7" :question/math-academy-id "e-14422" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle{\\int_{e}^{e^2} \\dfrac{\\ln^2 x}{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x}$." :question/worked-solution "Let's set $u = \\ln x$. Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}= \\dfrac 1 x\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm{d}u=\\dfrac 1 x\\,{\\textrm{d}x}\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}x & e & e^{2} \\\\ u & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\int_{e}^{e^2} \\dfrac{\\ln^2 x}{x}\\,\\textrm{d}x &= \\int_{e}^{e^2} (\\ln x)^2\\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}x}{x} \\\\[5pt] &=\\int_{1}^{2} u^2\\,\\textrm{d}u \\\\[5pt] &=\\left.\\dfrac13u^{3}\\right|_{1}^{2} \\\\[5pt] &=\\dfrac{1}{3}\\left(2^3-1^3 \\right) \\\\[5pt] &=\\dfrac{1}{3}\\left(8-1 \\right) \\\\[5pt] &=\\dfrac{7}{3} \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101057 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "41b7d83f-3b9b-556c-9e49-13df9c3b597e" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Functions Containing the Natural Logarithm"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "805b84a4-d27a-514e-a586-c2d6e38ad057" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln \\mid \\ln x \\mid + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098113} {:answer/id #uuid "c6443f24-a54f-599c-b46d-4a92ba5f6412" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\ln \\mid \\ln (2x) \\mid" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098114} {:answer/id #uuid "efa53843-32a8-5214-bb83-d2fb2520dd02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln \\mid \\ln (2x) \\mid + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098115} {:answer/id #uuid "1f